y regional eligibility first<!-- --> →</a></div></div></div></section></details></div></details><section class="v2-section v3-faq-section" id="compare-faq"><div class="nx-rule nx-rule--section" aria-hidden="true"><span class="nx-rule__label nx-rule__index"></span><span class="nx-rule__line"></span><span class="nx-rule__stamp">3</span></div><div class="v3-faq-card"><div class="v3-faq-card__header"><span class="v3-faq-card__eyebrow">FAQ &amp; decision checks</span><h2 class="v3-faq-card__title">Binance vs OKX: fees, product access and account checks</h2><p class="v3-faq-card__lead">Use these questions before opening either official registration route.</p></div><div class="v3-faq-list"><details class="v3-faq-item"><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="v3-compare-faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M9 8a3 3 0 1 1 5 2.2c-1.2.8-2 1.2-2 2.8M12 17h.01M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Z"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">OKX vs Binance: who has lower fees?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content">On spot fees, OKX has lower base fees (Binance 0.10% / 0.10%; OKX 0.08% / 0.10%, maker / taker). These are checked base-fee snapshots; verify account tiers, token discounts, rebates, funding and regional eligibility in the official account. Compare Binance and OKX by their official fee tables, product-specific availability, identity requirements, regional restrictions, Web3 or DEX-style access paths and announcement sources. Do not treat either public comparison as a current account entitlement, fee guarantee or eligibility decision.</div></details><details class="v3-faq-item"><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="v3-compare-faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M9 8a3 3 0 1 1 5 2.2c-1.2.8-2 1.2-2 2.8M12 17h.01M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Z"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">Is Binance vs OKX mainly a fee comparison?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content">Fees matter, but the safer comparison also checks product scope, KYC, regional eligibility, Web3 wallet or DEX-style routing, official announcements and the source date for each claim.</div></details><details class="v3-faq-item" hidden=""><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="v3-compare-faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M9 8a3 3 0 1 1 5 2.2c-1.2.8-2 1.2-2 2.8M12 17h.01M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Z"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">Can this page decide whether my account can trade a product?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content">No. It can narrow what to verify. Final access depends on the current official account flow, user region, verification status, product rules and platform terms.</div></details><button type="button" class="v3-faq-list__expand" aria-expanded="false">Show 1 more question<span aria-hidden="true"> ↓</span></button></div></div></section><details class="v2-section v3-compare-group v3-compare-group--before"><summary class="v3-compare-group__summary"><span>Before you register</span><b aria-hidden="true">＋</b></summary><div class="v3-compare-group__body"><section class="v2-section v3-compare-disclosure-section"><details class="research-references"><summary id="compare-sources">Must verify before registration</summary><section class="v2-section research-comparison" id="research-comparison"><div class="research-heading"><h2>Compare the details</h2><label class="research-differences"><input type="checkbox"/>Show differences only</label></div><table class="research-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Compare the details</th><th scope="col"><span translate="no" lang="en" dir="ltr"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--binance" src="/brands/tile/binance-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/binance-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/binance-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="binance" data-brand-source="verified"/>Binance</span></th><th scope="col"><span translate="no" lang="en" dir="ltr"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--okx" src="/brands/tile/okx-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/okx-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/okx-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="okx" data-brand-source="verified"/>OKX</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Products</th><td data-platform="Binance" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>The public fee page separates Spot &amp; Margin, NFT, P2P, and fiat-fee sections; derivative availability should be checked on product-specific Binance pages.<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored" lang="en" href="/go/binance-page?to=%2Fen%2Ffee%2Ftrading">Read source<!-- --> ↗</a></p></td><td data-platform="OKX" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>OKX navigation lists spot, futures, DEX, events/options, trading bots, copy trading, Earn, institutional APIs, and proof-of-reserves areas.<span lang="en" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com">Read source<span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fees</th><td data-platform="Binance" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>Spot fees are shown as maker/taker rates and tiered by 30-day trade volume and/or BNB balance.<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored" lang="en" href="/go/binance-page?to=%2Fen%2Ffee%2Ftrading">Read source<!-- --> ↗</a></p></td><td data-platform="OKX" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>The fees page separates spot, futures, options, and other trading instruments instead of using one blended fee claim.<span lang="en" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com">Read source<span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Account &amp; access</th><td data-platform="Binance" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>Binance says new users must complete Verified identity verification to access products including crypto deposits and trades.<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored" lang="en" href="/go/binance-page?to=%2Fen%2Fsupport%2Ffaq%2Fdetail%2F360027287111">Read source<!-- --> ↗</a></p></td><td data-platform="OKX" lang="en" dir="ltr"><p>The identity-verification support path is a required source before making registration, review-time, or supported-document statements.<span lang="en" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com">Read source<span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></section><div class="v3-deep-compare" style="--compare-columns:2"><div class="v3-deep-compare__head"><span>Dimension</span><span translate="no" lang="en"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--binance" src="/brands/tile/binance-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/binance-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/binance-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="binance" data-brand-source="verified"/>Binance</span><span translate="no" lang="en"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--okx" src="/brands/tile/okx-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/okx-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/okx-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="okx" data-brand-source="verified"/>OKX</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Platform type</b><span>CEX</span><span>CEX</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Access model</b><span>Account-based access; verify KYC, funding, and regional eligibility on the official domain</span><span>Account-based access; verify KYC, funding, and regional eligibility on the official domain</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Verified product scope</b><span>No verified coverage yet</span><span>No verified coverage yet</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Must verify before registration</b><span>Whether the current region can open an account and use the intended product / KYC tier, funding path, withdrawal limits, and account controls / Fee schedule, campaign terms, listing notice, and expiry from official sources</span><span>Current region, identity verification, and product eligibility / Whether fees, activities, listings, and product descriptions come from official pages / Whether the intended route is CEX account access or Web3/wallet access</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Best fit</b><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">Choose Binance when you need a broad account exchange with spot, margin, fiat, P2P and product-specific fee pages checked before signup.</span></span><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">Choose OKX when you want one account path that also exposes Web3, DEX, bots, copy trading, Earn and proof-of-reserves review areas.</span></span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Why choose it</b><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">The official sources separate fee tiers, BNB balance rules, identity verification and announcement checks, so the signup path can be reviewed in one place.</span></span><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">The fee source separates spot, futures, options and other instruments, while the navigation distinguishes exchange and Web3-style choices.</span></span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Not ideal for</b><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">Avoid treating it as universally available: identity verification, product access and regional rules still have to match the user&#x27;s account.</span></span><span><span lang="en" dir="ltr">Avoid treating Web3, DEX, Earn or copy trading as the same promise as an exchange account; each needs product, risk and region checks.</span></span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Verified official domain</b><span>www.binance.com</span><span>www.okx.com</span></div><div class="v3-deep-compare__row"><b>Activities/listings</b><span>28 · Binance Alpha Trading Competition: Trade Stable (STABLE) and Share $200K Worth of Rewards (2026-10-09)</span><span>20 · OKX to list Unified Tokenized Stocks XBRKB, XWEN and more for spot trading</span></div></div></details></section><details class="v2-section v3-similar v3-similar-disclosure"><summary class="section-lead v3-similar-disclosure__summary"><h2>Continue research</h2><span>Open platform detail links</span><b aria-hidden="true">＋</b></summary><div class="v3-similar-grid"><a href="/exchanges/binance"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--binance" src="/brands/tile/binance-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/binance-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/binance-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="binance" data-brand-source="verified"/><span translate="no" lang="en">Binance</span><small>Open independent profile</small></a><a href="/exchanges/okx"><img class="v2-brand v2-brand--compact v2-brand--tile v2-brand--okx" src="/brands/tile/okx-128.webp" srcSet="/brands/tile/okx-64.webp 64w, /brands/tile/okx-128.webp 128w" sizes="48px" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-brand-slug="okx" data-brand-source="verified"/><span translate="no" lang="en">OKX</span><small>Open independent profile</small></a></div><nav class="v3-compare-related" aria-label="Platform profiles" data-compare-related="curated"><div class="v3-compare-related__group"><strong class="v3-compare-related__label" lang="en">More comparisons with Binance</strong><ul class="v3-compare-related__list"><li><a href="/compare/aerodrome-vs-binance" translate="no" lang="en" data-growth