="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="vx-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M9.5 9a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 .5c0 2-2.5 2-2.5 4M12 17h.01"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">Is an OKX exchange account the same as OKX Wallet?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content"><p>No. OKX describes OKX Web3 Wallet as a non-custodial, multi-chain wallet: you hold the seed phrase or private key, the wallet needs no identity verification or account login, and a lost seed phrase cannot be recovered. The OKX exchange account is a separate sign-up that uses identity verification to raise deposit and withdrawal limits. A referral code belongs to the exchange account and must be added before that account is created.</p><p class="v3-venue-direct-answer__links"><span data-cta-kind="source" data-cta-placement="venue-faq-source" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com"><span>OKX — What is OKX Web3 Wallet</span><span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span><span data-cta-kind="source" data-cta-placement="venue-faq-source" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com"><span>OKX — Identity verification guide</span><span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span><span data-cta-kind="source" data-cta-placement="venue-faq-source" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com"><span>OKX — Referral program FAQ</span><span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></div></details><details class="v3-faq-item" hidden=""><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="vx-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M9.5 9a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 .5c0 2-2.5 2-2.5 4M12 17h.01"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">Where do I enter a OKX referral code?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content"><p>Check the prefilled code before completing sign-up. OKX says a previous referral link can remain associated with the device for 30 days.</p><p class="v3-venue-direct-answer__links"><span data-cta-kind="source" data-cta-placement="venue-faq-source" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com"><span>okx — Source</span><span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></div></details><details class="v3-faq-item" hidden=""><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="vx-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M9.5 9a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 .5c0 2-2.5 2-2.5 4M12 17h.01"></path></svg></span><span class="v3-faq-q-text">Can a OKX code be added after sign-up?</span></div><span class="v3-faq-arrow" aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="v3-faq-content"><p>The reviewed official help does not document adding a code after registration. This is unconfirmed, not proof that it is impossible.</p><p class="v3-venue-direct-answer__links"><span data-cta-kind="source" data-cta-placement="venue-faq-source" style="cursor:text" data-source-plain="okx.com"><span>okx — Source</span><span class="source-plain__domain"> · <!-- -->okx.com</span></span></p></div></details><details class="v3-faq-item" hidden=""><summary class="v3-faq-summary"><div class="v3-faq-summary-left"><span class="vx-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round